<Base title="Fretwork — AI & Systems for Small Teams · Vault Human" description="Fretwork builds practical AI and systems that modernize how the work gets done — without anyone losing themselves in the machinery. A Vault Human company.">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="pagehead">
<p class="eyebrow">Fretwork &middot; Technology</p>
<h1>Modernize the work &mdash; without losing the people in it.</h1>
<p class="dek">Practical AI and systems for small teams. Built to serve the humans doing the work, not replace them.</p>
</div>

<hr class="rule" />

<h2 class="sec">The problem</h2>
<div class="prose">
<p>Most teams are told to &ldquo;adopt AI&rdquo; and handed either hype or a tool that steamrolls how they actually work. The manual load stays. The people feel like an afterthought. And the modernization that was promised never quite arrives &mdash; or arrives at the cost of the very judgment that made the team good in the first place.</p>
</div>

<hr class="rule" />

<section>
<h2 class="sec">How Fretwork helps</h2>
<p class="turn" style="margin-bottom:26px">We don&rsquo;t automate people out. We build the machinery around them.</p>
<div class="coachcard">
<img src="/russ-michaels.jpg" alt="Russ Michaels, founder of Vault Human" width="120" height="150" />
<div><p class="coachname">Russ Michaels, Esq.</p><p class="coachrole">Founder &middot; Vault Human</p></div>
</div>
<div class="prose">
<p>Fretwork designs and builds practical AI and systems for small teams &mdash; the automations, workflows, and tools that take the manual weight off without anyone losing themselves in the machinery. Every build carries a human sign-off. The point isn&rsquo;t a flashier stack; it&rsquo;s people freed to do the work only they can do.</p>
</div>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<section>
<h2 class="sec">How it works</h2>
<ul class="steps">
<li><span class="rn">I</span><strong>A paid audit.</strong> We map how the work actually flows, and where the real friction lives.</li>
<li><span class="rn">II</span><strong>A build sprint.</strong> We build the specific automations and tools that remove it &mdash; with human QA on everything that ships.</li>
<li><span class="rn">III</span><strong>It runs.</strong> The team keeps the judgment; the machine carries the weight.</li>
</ul>
<div class="cta" style="margin-top:36px"><a class="btn-fill" href="#" data-open-form>Start with an audit</a></div>
</section>

<hr class="rule" />

<p class="note">Fretwork is one of four ways Vault Human holds a whole life. <a href="/" style="text-decoration:underline">See the others</a>.</p>
</div>
